       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily ibuprofen dose of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. That much raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common dose for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum daily dose\n- **1600 mg/day** divided some other way\n\nIf you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
